{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":68,"name":"Moniek Kuijpers","username":"moniek.kuijpers","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/moniek.kuijpers/{size}/23_2.png","created_at":"2021-10-19T17:01:00.824Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eDear all,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe, at IGEL, are proud to announce that our Handbook for Empirical Literary Studies is out. Each of our currently 21 research coalitions have written an overview chapter on their research area within the field of Empirical Literary Studies. The book is meant as an introduction for students or early career researchers into this rich - methodologically and theoretically - and ever expanding field.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can find more information on where to buy it or how to download it here:\u003c/p\u003e\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/9783110645958/html\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://www.degruyter.com/assets/images/ec7d7606b4e2f3f921b5e1700948efb6-favicon.ico\" class=\"site-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/9783110645958/html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eDe Gruyter\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:200/295;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//discourse.igelsociety.org/uploads/default/original/1X/e501b6d88490392a59d95e5e38132899bac9ce84.jpeg\" class=\"thumbnail\" width=\"200\" height=\"295\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/9783110645958/html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eHandbook of Empirical Literary Studies\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eThis handbook reviews efforts to increase the use of empirical methods in studies of the aesthetic and social effects of literary reading. The reviewed research is expansive, including extension of familiar theoretical models to novel domains (e.g.,...\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe thank Don Kuiken and Arthur Jacobs for their hard work in putting this impressive collection of essays together.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2021-10-20T15:17:35.062Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":29,"reads":18,"readers_count":17,"score":298.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":61,"topic_slug":"the-handbook-of-empirical-literary-studies-is-out","display_username":"Moniek Kuijpers","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/9783110645958/html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Handbook of Empirical Literary Studies","clicks":19}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":8,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"event":null,"calendar_details":[],"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"can_vote":false}],"stream":[68]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1808]],"suggested_topics":[{"id":846,"title":"PhD Vacancy Stavanger: Deep Reading in Higher Education","fancy_title":"PhD Vacancy Stavanger: Deep Reading in Higher Education","slug":"phd-vacancy-stavanger-deep-reading-in-higher-education","posts_count":1,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":1,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-02-03T10:30:59.964Z","last_posted_at":"2026-02-03T10:31:00.192